---
import Article from '../layouts/Article.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
---
<Article
  title="About SalaryLens"
  heading="About SalaryLens"
  description="SalaryLens is a free, no-sign-up in-hand salary calculator for India, built to make CTC transparent."
  path="/about/"
  showCta={false}
>
  <p>
    <strong>{SITE.name}</strong> is a free, no-sign-up tool that decodes any Indian CTC into your
    real monthly take-home pay. It exists because "CTC" is one of the most confusing numbers in an
    Indian job offer — and the gap between CTC and in-hand catches almost everyone off guard.
  </p>
  <p>
    The web calculator shares its tax engine with the <strong>SalaryLens Chrome extension</strong>,
    which shows estimated in-hand salary right on job posts on LinkedIn and Naukri. Everything is
    computed in your browser — no accounts, no salary data sent anywhere.
  </p>
  <p>
    Built by {SITE.author}. Start with the <a href={url('/')}>in-hand salary calculator</a>, or
    read the <a href={url('/methodology/')}>methodology</a> to see exactly how the numbers are
    derived.
  </p>
</Article>
